WEBVTT

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:40.180
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.340
Episode Three

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:56.340
"The Case of the Mt. Kurama Estate Inheritance"

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.590
<i>Holmes-san invited me to 
go hiking in Kurama today.</i>

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.810
Will this be your first time 
on Mt. Kurama, Aoi-san?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.850
Yes. I'm really looking forward to it!

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.350
I'm sorry. After all that...

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:15.880
Oh, you're going to Mt. Kurama?

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:19.780
Would you mind stopping by 
Kajiwara-sensei's mountain villa, then?

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:21.360
Your fellow novelist?

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.360
He passed away earlier this year, didn't he?

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:24.580
Yes.

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.660
It seems his family would like to ask 
for your help with something.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.410
Do you mind?

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.190
I don't mind, but...

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.670
Oh, I don't mind at all!

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.620
I'm sorry. To both of you.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.260
Oh, it's not quite an apology,

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.930
but you should eat at a 
kawadoko restaurant in Kibune.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.190
I'll make a reservation.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:53.940
Our special hiking trip turned 
into an errand for my father.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.670
That's okay...

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.470
It's not every day you get 
to eat lunch at a Kibune kawadoko

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.900
and visit a writer's mountain villa.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.440
I really can't wait.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:07.380
You're too kind, Aoi-san.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:12.950
Aoi-san.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:14.830
Look at that!

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.220
What is that?

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.970
It's a happiness strap. They say that if 
you grab it, it will bring you happiness.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.310
A happiness strap?

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.860
Aoi-san?

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.480
Sorry...

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:46.490
Wow! The Momiji Tunnel!

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:49.590
I see taking the train was the right idea.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.240
Yes! It's like I'm on a real vacation!

00:03:54.230 --> 00:03:57.600
<i>Though it really feels more
 like a pick-me-up trip...</i>

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:00.500
That's right.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.620
Well, let's enjoy the vacation.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:05.750
You're so right!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.480
<b>Water Fortune Omikuji</b>

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.480
<b>Best Luck</b>

00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:31.970
This is wonderful!

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:35.990
I'm glad I invited you.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:39.250
You've seemed rather listless lately.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:44.000
As usual, you see right through me, Holmes-san...

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:48.390
I was thinking you must have saved 
up the money to go to Saitama by now.

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:54.020
Yes... but each time I think 
about going, I hesitate.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.180
I can understand that.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:58.670
At times like this, 
it's best to do what comes naturally,

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.330
rather than trying to 
force yourself to action.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.880
Thank you very much.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:09.770
But I'm a little surprised that 
you understand how I feel.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.290
To be perfectly honest,

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:17.690
your discerning eye wasn't the only 
reason I asked you to work at Kura.

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:19.790
There was another reason.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.810
The truth is... 
I've been through the same thing.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.930
I lost my girlfriend to someone else.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:31.120
When I was in my third year of high school,

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.690
I was in a relationship 
with a girl in my grade.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:36.280
At the time, I took everything very seriously,

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.630
and I'd sworn to myself that,
 for both of our sakes,

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.850
we should remain chaste until 
after entrance exams were over.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:46.360
I was keeping our relationship pure in a 
way that would not shame the Kiyotaka name.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:49.210
<i>Is his given name special somehow?</i>

00:05:49.210 --> 00:05:53.450
But I think she started 
feeling lonely around me.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.990
Once we were in college, she was quickly

00:05:56.990 --> 00:06:02.000
swept off her feet by an arrogant 
and overbearing Osakan.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.260
But because I went through that, 
I can understand how you feel.

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.090
Aoi-san?

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.720
Oh, it's nothing. I was just surprised...

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.680
It felt kind of... 
"Wow, Holmes-san is so normal."

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:21.770
What is that supposed to mean?

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.770
S-Sorry...

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:29.600
It seems she's going to marry that 
arrogant and overbearing Osakan.

00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:35.790
But when I heard that news, 
for some reason, it came as a relief.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:39.420
A relief? Why?

00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:43.720
"If they were so meant for each other
 that they're joining in matrimony,

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:46.420
then it was destiny that she would leave me."

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.590
It freed me to think of it that way.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:50.270
Destiny?

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:57.930
So rather than forcing a decision, you may 
be better served by leaving it to destiny.

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.110
Maybe so.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.390
That was so delicious!

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.550
I need to thank the manager.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.050
I suppose we should take care 
of business for him, then.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.200
Okay!

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:21.180
Kajiwara-sensei's secretary, Kurashina-san, 
will escort us to the villa.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:31.210
I am Kajiwara's wife, Ayako.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:53.010
A pleasure to meet you. 
I am Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.620
A-And I'm Mashiro Aoi.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.620
A pleasure. I'm the eldest, Fuyuki.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.710
The third son, Haruhiko.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:04.040
Second son, Akihito.

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.430
You attend Kyoto University, Kiyotaka-san?

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:13.090
Yes, though I entered in graduate school.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.630
I was at Kyoto Prefectural before then.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:21.180
Kyoto Prefectural? Our Haruhiko 
is a second-year there now.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:24.320
Maybe I'll try to get into Kyoto U, too!

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.390
Kyoto Prefectural, Kyoto U...

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.620
It's like a different world to me.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:34.370
That's because you ran off
 to become an actor.

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:37.190
You're an actor, Akihito-san?

00:08:37.190 --> 00:08:40.250
The rising star of AK Company.

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.930
Ever seen me on TV?

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:44.720
S-Sorry...

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.620
You've got a ways to go, Akihito.

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.840
Holmes-san?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:51.270
Is something the matter?

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:55.410
No... I was thinking
 the resemblance is striking.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.460
<i>Resemblance? Between who?</i>

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:02.680
Now... what did you wish to discuss?

00:09:03.550 --> 00:09:06.700
Allow me to explain.

00:09:07.180 --> 00:09:13.090
When Kajiwara-sensei died, 
I was given two wills.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:25.370
<b>Will</b>

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:18.010
The first was regarding 
the division of assets,

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:20.920
but the second contained a request that

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:24.350
I open it here at the Mt. Kurama 
villa three months later.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:27.090
I opened it the other day.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:31.530
It contained instructions to bestow a set 
of his treasured art pieces to his sons,

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.970
as well as a code to a safe.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:37.240
Inside the safe were three hanging scrolls.

00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:40.660
Hanging scrolls, you say?

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:45.440
Yes. But when I had 
an appraiser look at them,

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:50.720
he said that they were reproductions 
with no artistic value.

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.240
Then why...

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:56.000
Actually, that's not even the real problem.

00:09:56.460 --> 00:10:00.990
The truth is... someone burned the scrolls.

00:10:04.140 --> 00:10:06.890
Someone burned the scrolls?

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:12.050
Yes. All three were burned 
in the incinerator here.

00:10:12.390 --> 00:10:14.190
Who would do something so awful?

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:15.930
Who else?

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:18.220
It was somebody in this room.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:22.140
It's true that the only ones who could 
have burned the scrolls that night

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:24.030
are the people who live here.

00:10:24.030 --> 00:10:25.180
See?

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.760
Then the appraiser, Yanagihara-sensei, 
told me that Ijuin-sensei's son

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:33.940
was also known as "Holmes," 
so I asked for an introduction.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.360
I see. So it was Yanagihara-sensei...

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.720
You know him?

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:39.500
He's an old friend of my grandfather's.

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:40.960
Oh, the owner!

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:43.190
So, Kiyotaka-san, is it?

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:45.710
You'd better catch us that culprit!

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:49.070
If you call yourself Holmes, 
you'd better be something special.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:53.960
I'm only called "Holmes" because 
my last name is Yagashira, actually.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.970
So there's no way you can help us, right?

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.840
Not so. I actually have an idea
of who did it already.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:03.710
Really?

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:09.590
But I have no proof just yet, 
so I'd like to speak with each of you.

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:10.730
Very well.

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.840
I'll start with Fuyuki-san.

00:11:13.220 --> 00:11:14.110
Certainly.

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:18.280
How do you feel about 
your share of the estate?

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.830
H-Holmes-san!

00:11:19.830 --> 00:11:20.850
I don't mind.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:24.120
Regarding the inheritance, 
my primary thought was, "Ah, of course."

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.610
My father was quite a spendthrift.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:27.880
Yeah, no kidding...

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:31.620
At the same time, he had 
a very strong sense of obligation.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:34.740
I see.

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:39.070
Then would you tell me about 
the scroll that was left to you?

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:39.970
Yes.

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.610
I think it was like...

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:50.400
Taira no Kiyomori in a golden kimono, 
holding a large fan up to a red sun.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.400
I see. "Kiyomori Calls Back the Setting Sun."

00:11:54.140 --> 00:11:55.390
Was it this?

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:57.570
Yes!

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.070
<i>That's the Holmes-san I know! 
He sure works fast.</i>

00:12:01.070 --> 00:12:04.400
Fuyuki-san, what did you 
think about your scroll?

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:08.670
I just figured my father liked Kiyomori...

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:10.650
Thank you very much.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:14.170
Next, Akihito-san. 
The same question, if you would.

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.540
I was pretty surprised by my inheritance.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:20.930
He basically treated me 
like the prodigal son.

00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.660
I'm honestly surprised I got any—

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:25.800
Very well. Now, about the scroll...

00:12:25.800 --> 00:12:28.460
Um, I think it was by Hokusai.

00:12:28.460 --> 00:12:31.050
It was mostly an unpainted background 
with a dragon and Mt. Fuji—

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:31.550
This?

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.820
"Dragon Flying Over Mt. Fuji."

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:35.570
Yeah...

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:38.060
Lastly, your feelings about the scroll?

00:12:38.660 --> 00:12:41.380
I guess... it made me pretty happy?

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:42.780
I like Hokusai, and—

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.030
Next, Haruhiko-san.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:44.580
Yes?

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.330
Hey!

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:46.830
Yes? What's the matter?

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:49.960
Why are you being so rude to me?

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:51.830
My, what a strange reaction!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.310
After you insulted me first...

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.960
What a funny person you are.

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:57.800
H-Hey!

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.450
<i>There it goes! Holmes-san's 
trademark nastiness!</i>

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.140
<i>But I wonder why it's all targeted at him...</i>

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.040
<i>Could it be...?</i>

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:15.500
That's right. I'm not fond of superficial, 
arrogant, overbearing men.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.240
<i>In other words, like that other guy...</i>

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:22.230
Now, as for you, Haruhiko-san...

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.690
Yes, Senpai.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.770
To be honest, 
my first thought was, "Is that all?"

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:30.000
"I thought we had more money than that."

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.790
What did you think about your 
father, Kajiwara-sensei?

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:37.000
Was he strict? Was he lenient?

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:39.760
My father was always very kind.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.950
Haruhiko-san, what did you think 
when you looked at your scroll?

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:46.770
I didn't really understand it...

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:47.880
What do you mean?

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:51.160
It wasn't something that sent 
a clear message at a glance.

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.150
I think it was... Taira no Tadamori?

00:13:55.870 --> 00:14:01.560
Was it a picture of a warrior leader 
and a priest holding a lantern?

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:04.640
Yes, that was it exactly!

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:06.370
I see.

00:14:07.290 --> 00:14:08.650
Thank you very much.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.530
Ayako-san.

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.400
Could I ask you a question?

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:13.030
Of course.

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:17.600
Did you know that your husband 
left those scrolls behind?

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.050
No, I had no idea.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.550
Did he leave anything to you?

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:24.590
No, nothing for me...

00:14:24.590 --> 00:14:27.370
Oh, but before he passed, 
he did give me this.

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:29.540
An aquamarine?

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:31.800
You recognize it?

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:36.650
What did you think about the paintings 
your husband left to your sons?

00:14:36.650 --> 00:14:40.420
Well... I had assumed they 
were part of the inheritance,

00:14:40.420 --> 00:14:43.140
so I was surprised to learn 
that they were worthless.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.570
Thank you very much.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:46.910
Lastly, Kurashina-san...

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:47.580
Yes?

00:14:48.100 --> 00:14:50.580
How did you become his secretary?

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:56.840
Well, it's a little embarrassing 
to talk about it...

00:14:56.840 --> 00:15:00.090
The truth is, I used to be in a biker gang.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:03.670
Surprising, isn't it?

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.210
Especially since he's gone so straight since...

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:11.680
When I was young and Sensei was 
still a lawyer, he helped me out.

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:14.470
We'd been close ever since.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:18.520
Then after a certain incident, 
I became his secretary.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.740
An incident?

00:15:19.740 --> 00:15:24.110
He saved my husband's life.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:25.220
His life?

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.110
Yes.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:29.380
He got into an argument with a gang 
he'd based one of his novels on.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:31.000
They attacked him.

00:15:31.670 --> 00:15:34.600
And the one who risked
 their life to save him then...

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:38.860
was Kurashina-san.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:41.030
I see...

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:43.360
That concludes my questions.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.630
This is rather difficult...

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:53.690
It's important to identify the culprit,

00:15:54.170 --> 00:16:00.140
but I think I'll start by explaining why 
Kajiwara-sensei left you those scrolls.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.530
What does that mean?

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:04.150
Have you figured something out?

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.270
Yes.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:09.900
There was a message for each of his 
sons in the scrolls he left behind.

00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:15.240
"Kiyomori Calls Back the Setting Sun"
 is an expression of the extent

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:20.580
of Taira no Kiyomori's power, so great 
that he could move even the setting sun.

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:27.180
With this painting, I believe Kajiwara-sensei 
was telling you to aim for great heights,

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:31.950
as Kiyomori did, without 
succumbing to the same hubris.

00:16:33.490 --> 00:16:36.560
Is that... how he felt?

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:40.620
I had no idea... I was such a fool...

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:46.320
And? Well... What about mine, then, Holmes-san?

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:51.010
The "Dragon Flying Over Mt. Fuji" painting
 he gave to you was Hokusai's final work.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.460
Before he passed, Hokusai said,

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:58.090
"If I could have lived five years more, 
I could have become a true artist."

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:02.340
That picture was an expression 
of Hokusai's ambition,

00:17:02.340 --> 00:17:05.570
depicted as a dragon 
trying to fly over Mt. Fuji.

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:09.820
I believe Kajiwara-sensei was telling you 
that if you truly wish to pursue your art,

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:12.090
to aim high like Hokusai did.

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:17.340
To let your star rise like 
a dragon soaring to the heavens.

00:17:17.730 --> 00:17:21.960
He may not have said it out loud, 
but I believe he wanted you to succeed.

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:29.670
Dad...

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:34.860
And the last, Haruhiko-san's scroll...

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:35.860
Stop it!

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:42.370
I... I burned them.

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:43.520
Mom?!

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:44.900
What are you talking about?

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:46.500
Why would you do that?

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.630
Because...

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:50.090
I... I was angry.

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.380
Angry that the second will 
didn't say anything about me...

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:55.720
Over that?

00:17:55.720 --> 00:18:00.540
But... I didn't realize that the 
scrolls had messages like that.

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.220
I'm sorry.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.880
So we can stop this now, can't we?

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:05.490
Mom...

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:09.190
That solves the mystery.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:11.680
Let's go home, Aoi-san.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.500
H-Holmes-san?

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.670
Wait!

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:23.700
I believe my job is finished here.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.170
But we didn't get to hear
 about Haruhiko's painting.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:30.450
You might wish you hadn't.

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:32.540
I don't mind.

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:38.810
Very well.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:43.300
That painting is based on a tale
 known as "Tadamori's Lantern."

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:48.060
One day, Taira no Tadamori was tasked by 
his master, the former emperor Shirakawa,

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:51.770
to slay a monster that appeared to be an oni.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:56.430
But he captured it alive 
to ascertain its true nature,

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:58.860
and revealed it to be 
an elderly monk of Gion.

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:02.300
The former emperor thanked 
Tadamori for not killing the monk

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:05.380
over a mistaken identity, 
and gave him a reward.

00:19:05.910 --> 00:19:08.870
But that is not the heart of the matter.

00:19:09.600 --> 00:19:15.020
Many believe that the reward given to 
Tadamori was the former emperor's beloved,

00:19:15.020 --> 00:19:18.890
Gion no Nyogo, and that 
Taira no Kiyomori was born thereafter.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:22.640
H-Holmes-san, you mean...

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.690
H-Hang on a sec...

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:27.890
That means what Mom was trying to hide was...

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:31.400
Are you saying that 
Kajiwara-sensei learned about

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:35.320
Kurashina-san's feelings for Ayako-san, 
and after saving his life...

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:39.470
He... let him have Ayako-san, 
like in the story?

00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.470
But that's so...

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:47.780
Ayako-san didn't want it known, I'm sure.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.710
Especially to you two.

00:19:50.320 --> 00:19:53.970
Why didn't you take that shit 
to the grave, you old bastard?!

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:57.040
If I may, and this is just my hypothesis, but...

00:19:57.040 --> 00:20:00.750
Did Haruhiko-san only recently turn 20?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:04.290
Y-Yeah, just before the second will was opened...

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.190
Is that it?

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:13.700
Yes. Sensei surely intended to tell 
Haruhiko-san the truth when he came of age.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.930
That is why he chose that as the 
date the will would be opened.

00:20:18.380 --> 00:20:20.650
This is nuts...

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:26.920
If that's true... you think Dad 
was holding a grudge against Mom?

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:29.160
I don't believe that's the case.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.330
How do you know?!

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:32.320
The ring?

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:35.900
Yes. The aquamarine he gave Ayako-san.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.580
It's a stone that represents freedom.

00:20:38.580 --> 00:20:40.210
Freedom...

00:20:40.970 --> 00:20:47.380
After his death, he surely wanted Ayako-san 
to be free to live her own life.

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:48.890
I... I see.

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:50.220
Of course...

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:55.500
Understood. We'll find a good time 
and tell Mom and Haruhiko about it.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:56.950
I'll take you to the station.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:00.230
When did you realize the truth?

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:02.210
Let me see...

00:21:02.210 --> 00:21:05.500
The moment I saw Haruhiko-san, I believe.

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:09.600
Akihito-san, eyes front! Eyes front!

00:21:10.060 --> 00:21:12.970
A-Are you serious? What gives?

00:21:12.970 --> 00:21:14.670
It was the ears.

00:21:14.670 --> 00:21:15.630
Ears?

00:21:15.630 --> 00:21:20.120
Yes. Kurashina-san and Haruhiko-san's 
ears were identical.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:24.130
Only blood relatives can have identical ears.

00:21:24.620 --> 00:21:29.340
So I thought that Ayako-san and 
Kurashina-san might be having an affair.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:31.770
Is that a problem?

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:35.510
Boy, you really are something.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.510
Fine, I accept it... You <i>are</i> Holmes.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:43.160
I've been a real Sherlockian 
since I was a kid.

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:47.790
I got pretty annoyed at the idea of some 
jerk swinging the Holmes name around,

00:21:47.790 --> 00:21:50.030
but you're pretty interesting.

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:52.890
You are quite entertaining yourself.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:54.550
Although you're a type 
I find deeply unpleasant.

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:56.640
Unpleasant?!

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:59.800
Please, Akihito-san! Eyes front!

00:22:00.360 --> 00:22:04.100
You can't be that upset.
I'm simply repeating what you told me earlier.

00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:05.390
You shut up!

00:22:06.300 --> 00:23:36.390
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
"After the Festival"

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
Next Episode

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.410
It's nice to be able to work in a yukata...

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:43.650
Aoi-san, why are you on the verge of tears?

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:46.390
Next time: "After the Festival."

00:23:46.870 --> 00:23:49.660
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
